Basic Network Scanning with Nmap

Objective

The objective of this task is to perform a basic network scan using Nmap and identify open ports and services running on a local machine.

Tools Used

- Nmap
- Command Prompt
- official website:

https://nmap.org/

Steps Performed

1. Installed Nmap

Downloaded and installed Nmap from the official website.

2. Identified Local IP Address

Used the following command:

ipconfig

3. Performed Basic Scan

nmap 192.168.1.5

4. Performed Service Version Scan

nmap -sV 192.168.1.5

5. Saved Results to File

nmap -sV 192.168.1.5 > nmap_scan_results.txt

Open Ports and Services Found

Port| Service| Description
135| MSRPC| Microsoft Remote Procedure Call
139| NetBIOS| File and printer sharing
445| Microsoft-DS| SMB file sharing service

Significance of Open Ports

- Port 135 is used for Windows remote communication.
- Port 139 is used for file and printer sharing services.
- Port 445 is used for SMB communication and file sharing.

Files Included

- nmap_scan_results.txt
- Screenshots of scan results
- README.md

Conclusion

Successfully performed a basic network scan using Nmap and identified open ports and services running on the local machine.
